; WinLlama 3.x module definition file.
;
; Note: OpenWatcom's wlink does not consume .def files directly -- it
; has its own native directive language (NAME/FILE/OPTION/EXPORT/
; SYSTEM). The STACKSIZE setting below is what actually matters for
; this project, and it's applied via "option stack=16384" on the
; wlink command line in the makefile, not by this file. This .def is
; kept as the conventional, portable record of the project's linker
; settings -- e.g. it would be picked up as-is by a genuine
; .def-consuming linker (Microsoft LINK, Borland TLINK/ILINK32) if
; this project is ever rebuilt with a different 16-bit toolchain.
;
; No EXPORTS section: DialogProcedure is declared static (internal
; linkage, correct -- nothing outside winllama.c calls it by name) and
; is only ever passed to CreateDialog() as a callback pointer. It does
; not need, and cannot have, a public export record; __export requires
; external linkage, which contradicts static (this combination is what
; produced the DIALOGPROCEDURE undefined-reference link error).
NAME        WINLLAMA
DESCRIPTION 'WinLlama 3.x - a Windows 3.1 Ollama client'
EXETYPE     WINDOWS
STUB        'WINSTUB.EXE'
CODE        PRELOAD MOVEABLE DISCARDABLE
DATA        PRELOAD MOVEABLE MULTIPLE
HEAPSIZE    2048
STACKSIZE   16384
